# Top-level requirements for the NOOA sandbox image's dependency tree.
#
# Compiled to sandbox-requirements.lock, which is what the profile installs from.
# This file states intent; the lock states what actually gets installed, with
# hashes. Regenerate with:
#
#   ./stage-lock.sh          (resolves inside the pinned base image, by digest)
#
# Why a lock at all. Pinning these four lines alone left every transitive
# dependency floating: `packaging` moved 26.2 -> 26.3 between two runs an hour
# apart, which changed the staged tree's content hash and therefore the image tag.
# The dependency set was recorded but not reproducible, so "same image" was only
# ever true within a session.
nooa==0.0.8
mcp==2.0.0
uvicorn==0.52.1

# The Ratify Python SDK. Until v1.0.0-alpha.16 is published it is installed
# separately from this checkout with --no-deps, so it is deliberately absent from
# this file; its own runtime requirements are listed below so they are locked
# rather than resolved at build time.
#
# RELEASE GATE: once alpha.16 is on PyPI, uncomment the pin below and regenerate
# the lock with ./stage-lock.sh. The final evidence has to be produced from the
# published package, because an image built from the checkout proves the checkout
# and not the artifact a reader installs.
#
# ratify-protocol==1.0.0a16
